        "original_id": "0cfec44b-9732-55ea-9018-48d39b7b5fd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Paulownia, Dendromecon\n- Animals: Endoclita excrescens\n- Taxonomy: genera, species, families\n- Places: California, northern Baja California\n\nFacts:\n- Paulownia is a genus of six to 17 species of flowering plants, depending on the taxonomic authority.\n- Paulownia belongs to the family Paulowniaceae and is related to, and sometimes included in, Scrophulariaceae.\n- Dendromecon, called the tree poppy, is a genus of one or two species of shrubs to small trees.\n- Dendromecon is native to California and northern Baja California.\n- Endoclita excrescens uses Castanea, Nicotiana, Paulownia, Quercus, and Raphanus as food plants.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
